\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Distributed In-Memory Data Storage and Loader
\f1\fs24 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs32 \cf3 \strokec3 Introduction
\f2\b\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 You are tasked with implementing a distributed key-value storage and loading system. Each record must be uniquely owned and stored on a single partition or node without replication. The objective is to achieve an even distribution of data across all available (mock) nodes in the cluster.
\f1\fs24 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa106\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs32 \cf3 \strokec3 Workflow
\f2\b\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 The loading process consists of the following steps:
\f1\fs24 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Schema Setup: Use config file to specify the schema, consider data types: string, int32.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Data Preparation: Prepare a data file on some or all mock nodes in the cluster, at least 100MB for each file, and may have duplication.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Cluster Start: Start server processes on all mock nodes in the cluster.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Local Reading: Every node reads a local data file existing on some or all cluster nodes.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	5	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Record Transfer: Nodes store local records or transfer them to the specific node that owns that record based on the distribution logic.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	6	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Statistics: Once the load job finishes, the system must print statistics, including the total number of records loaded per node.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	7	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Verification: Provide output confirming successful loading and evidence that records are stored on their corresponding owned nodes.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa106\partightenfactor0

